1. Works best running the scripts from the wfcrl-benchmark folder.
2. Need to make sure that the sizes of neural networks used for training matches that in the eval file.
3. Need a minimum number of timesteps≈3000 for IPPO/MAPPO to save properly. (Otherwise get "ValueError: Shape of passed values is (7, 1), indices imply (7, 7)") - Useful for doing short, debugging, runs.
4. At 10,000 iterations, episode length 100:
                        IDQN, IDRQN, and QMIX are really bad.
                        IPPO, and MAPPO are bad but better
                        IFAC and IFPPO are suprisingly good (they take longer to run) but they do not work in an episodic way. By ≈5000 iterations they both look good. IFPPO has maybe 
                        a slightly higher yield but initially more unstable yaw outputs. They both appear to produce similar optimal yaws.
